    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44073" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐθῡν-τήριος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>making straight: directing, ruling</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκῆπτρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					764
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐθυντηρία, ἡ</span>, <i>the part of a ship wherein the rudder was
				fixed</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				1356
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>base, plinth, socle</i> of a wall, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1668.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BCH</u>
				26.43
			</span></i> (Delph.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IGRom.</u>
				4.293a
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				i38
			</span></i> (Pergam., <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ.:
				τὸ ἐν τῷ ἐδάφει σύμμαγμα ὑπὸ τῶν
			ἀρχιτεκτόνων</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τήριον, τό</span>, <i>rule,
			norm</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γνώμων καὶ εὐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Theol.Ar.</u>
				59
			</span></i>.</div>
